# Build context exclusions for root-context image builds
# (`docker build -f container/Dockerfile .`, `hf/builder/Dockerfile`).
#
# Everything listed here is either regenerated inside the image or is
# host-specific state that must never be baked in. Trimming the context
# keeps `docker build` from shipping hundreds of MB to the daemon/builder
# on every run, and — more importantly — stops a host `node_modules`
# (built for the host's arch/platform) from landing on top of the
# `npm ci` tree the frontend stage just installed.

# VCS / CI metadata
.git
.github
.gitignore

# Node
**/node_modules
**/.npm
**/npm-debug.log*
**/.turbo
**/.vite
**/.next

# Build outputs (regenerated by the frontend stage)
**/dist
**/build
**/out
desktop/release

# Python
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.egg-info
**/.venv
**/venv

# Local runtime state / secrets — never bake these into an image.
# `*.example` templates are checked in and carry no secrets, so they stay.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.*.example
data/
outputs/
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.db

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
